138
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:32,140
Copy that.

139
00:05:32,140 --> 00:05:56,140
I can't get enough of the way the soy sauce smells!

140
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:57,140
I'm happy for you.

141
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:58,140
Well, hello!

142
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:00,140
Hey, Lukua and Shota.

143
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:01,140
Good evening!

144
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:02,340
Good evening.

145
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:05,220
Festivals are the best, aren't they?

146
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:05,800
Sure.

147
00:06:06,260 --> 00:06:08,320
Though they are a little different here.

148
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:12,380
In our world, many festivals were held to celebrate a lot of different gods.

149
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:13,420
Oh, wow.

150
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:16,340
No one really celebrates their religion around here anymore.

151
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:20,300
Celebrating the gods made security tight, which is why the dragons couldn't get close.

152
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:21,380
Oh, yeah.

153
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:25,280
In the big country up north, they held a huge festival in the spring every year.

154
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:27,360
It was so hard to get through there that season.

155
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:29,440
The gods actually came down the place.

156
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,380
Blah, blah, blah.

157
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:31,940
Uh, that's all I can hear.

158
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:36,400
I mean, I like hearing about other worlds, but it also makes me feel kind of invisible.

159
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:38,620
Oh, well, whatever.

160
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,420
It's fine.

161
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:42,020
Got it.

162
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:42,580
Yay!

163
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:47,200
Kana, your yukata is so cute!

164
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:50,600
Thank you, Saikawa.

165
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:51,700
So is yours.

166
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,820
Here's an idea.

167
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:59,120
Let's come to the festival together next year.

168
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:03,720
We can do it every year until we're little old ladies together, too.

169
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:09,820
Saikawa, please live a long time.

170
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:10,240
What?

171
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:11,840
I hope to.

172
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:16,220
You and I are BFFs forever, right?

173
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:17,360
That's so cool!

174
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:22,100
Yes!

175
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:23,100
Wow!

176
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:24,660
They're all so happy.

177
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:26,760
What a great place for kids.

178
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:32,260
I always forget you're not really a kid, and then every once in a while, bang, you act way more grown up than me.

179
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:34,260
Come on!

180
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,300
Come on!

181
00:07:36,980 --> 00:07:39,980
Takei, I was actually tricked into being here.

182
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,380
What does that mean?

183
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:47,060
I was told I had to be an adult, and that I could never go back to being a kid.

184
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,700
But Kobayashi encouraged me.

185
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,160
She said it was okay to be a kid again.

186
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:55,900
Wow.

187
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:59,500
And yet the more mature version of you is still there.

188
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:00,900
You think so?

189
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:03,940
If giving you permission is all it takes, then count me in.

190
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,980
I say you can be a kid, too.

191
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:06,600
Bam!

192
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:09,680
Yeah!

193
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:12,360
Well then, guess it's my turn.

194
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:14,380
I'm gonna make you an adult.

195
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:17,340
Wait, what the heck do you mean by that?

196
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:18,240
Made you look.

197
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:18,800
Wow.

198
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:21,200
That doesn't count, suck.

199
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:24,600
I think those who knew the old you would be so surprised to see you now.

200
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:28,680
You're one to talk, since when do goddesses become familiars?

201
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:29,720
Okay, sure.

202
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,720
Axe goddess, but you know what I mean.

203
00:08:32,060 --> 00:08:34,420
I simply do what I want, just like I always have.

204
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:36,340
If you're not having fun, you're not living.

205
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,480
Yeah, true.

206
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:40,080
So do you have feelings for Lukua?

207
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:42,200
Where'd that come from?

208
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:43,100
Who knows.

209
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:47,520
But for example, what if Lukua was hanging all over your friends or classmates,

210
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,620
and there was nothing you could do but watch them?

211
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:52,200
What would be going through your mind if that happened?

212
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:58,120
Hey, I'm sorry.

213
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,120
You don't have to say anything.

214
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:00,020
I think I get it.

215
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:02,460
That's what I thought.

216
00:09:02,620 --> 00:09:04,120
He'd be horrifically uncomfortable.

217
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,260
Wait, where are you going?

218
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:11,080
I stayed for an hour.

219
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:19,700
I was just about to look for you, Miss Kobayashi.

220
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:21,840
Oh, you look good in that one.

221
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,720
Aw, thank you so much!

222
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:25,680
Is everyone over there?

223
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:26,180
Hey.

224
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,480
Do you want to take a walk?

225
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:35,640
Just you and me?

226
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,460
I would love to!

227
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:46,600
What's gotten into you, Miss Kobayashi?

228
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:51,400
Have you finally come to appreciate my unique and powerful charms?

229
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:53,620
What?

230
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:58,260
You're one of the strongest dragons, even capable of fighting the gods.

231
00:09:58,480 --> 00:10:01,960
But here you're able to make friends with anyone whenever you feel like it.

232
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:07,040
Lately, I've been wondering, after hearing everything you've been through in the past,

233
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:11,060
how am I worthy of being loved by such an incredible person?

234
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:13,480
You've really been thinking about that?

235
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:17,160
I suppose I did share a few too many heavy stories.

236
00:10:17,660 --> 00:10:21,260
Here you are living with me like you never used to fear and hate humans.

237
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:25,140
You must be constantly reminded of the many things you had to go through.

238
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:28,300
Oh yeah, and you're also a dragon, so there's that.

239
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:31,220
That's what keeps repeating in my head.

240
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,180
So what?

241
00:10:33,180 --> 00:10:36,860
Anyway, I guess it's fine.

242
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:39,460
Even though it's a pain in the A sometimes.

243
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:44,280
Anyway, that's been my dilemma.

244
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:47,880
But what about you, Toru?

245
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:49,080
What's on your mind?

246
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,760
Want to know about my feelings?

247
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:55,040
Well, you know I love you, Miss Kobayashi.

248
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:57,920
I feel this way even though you're just a human.

249
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:01,020
And even though we are better than you.

250
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:02,920
Better than all humans, really.

251
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:05,260
I'm sure you're not surprised.

252
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,840
I am a dragon, and I take pride in that.

253
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:11,400
I've been places where you have to risk your life

254
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:13,820
and put everything on the line to prove your superiority.

255
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,920
But my heart...

256
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:19,860
When it came to love, I had no idea how to prove my feelings.

257
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:23,260
I wondered, would it be easier if I were a better fighter?

258
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:24,560
Or smarter?

259
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:27,220
I wished I could be those things.

260
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:30,740
I spent so much time trying to convince everyone I was.

261
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:32,840
I guess I was trying to be an adult.

262
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:35,680
But I realized I didn't have to try to be anything.

263
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,360
It was okay to just be myself.

264
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:43,300
And you're the one who helped me realize that, Miss Kobayashi.

265
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:46,640
You're giving me too much credit again.

266
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:50,540
I think it's a good sign that you're so unaware of it yourself.

267
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:54,780
Because it means you were meant to save me whether you wanted to or not.

268
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:59,420
Miss Kobayashi, I love you so much!

269
00:11:59,420 --> 00:11:59,440
Miss Kobayashi, I love you so much!

